Implement user story AMSD-2041: [GO, UP, MX] Live Preview of Content in CMS

## Story Description
AS a Content Author, I WANT to preview draft entries in CMS, SO THAT I can see how content will be shown on the website. This requires integrating Contentstack's Live Preview SDK for a Next.js CSR (Pages Router) application: adding a live_preview config block (enable, host) to the Stack initialization in src/services/contentstack.ts, installing and initializing @contentstack/live-preview-utils on the client side in src/pages/_app.tsx, wiring the onEntryChange callback to trigger a re-render through the existing ContentstackContext/useContent pipeline (note: per Contentstack documentation, onEntryChange takes no arguments — the re-render relies on the SDK's internal state update, not a callback parameter), and documenting the live_preview.enable and live_preview.host environment variables in .env.local.sample. Custom preview URL patterns are configured in the Contentstack dashboard (Settings > Stack > Live Preview), not via application environment variables. Limitation: Protected pages may not be previewable because the authentication gate cannot be bypassed by preview parameters.

## Acceptance Criteria
- 


## Root Cause Analysis & Prescribed Fix (AUTHORITATIVE — start here, do not re-trace)
A code investigation already traced this bug to its cause and prescribed the minimal fix below. This is the plan of record. Apply it; do NOT re-read the whole codebase to re-derive it.

The Acceptance Criteria above describe the desired END BEHAVIOR to VERIFY — they are NOT an implementation blueprint. Do not re-architect, split values, or add new fields/abstractions to satisfy an AC literally when the prescribed minimal fix already makes that AC pass. Implement the fix below; the ACs are how you check you got it right.

HARD RULES:
- Make the SMALLEST change that fixes the root cause. Fewer lines of code is always better.
- REUSE existing functions. Before writing any new helper, search the repo for an existing util/parser/formatter that already does what you need (use the CodeGraph tool documented below) and call it. Writing novel code when a helper already exists is a defect to be rejected in review.
- **src/services/contentstack.ts** (`options`): This is the Contentstack Delivery SDK initialization config. The `live_preview` block must be added here (management_token, enable, host) and CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW_TOKEN / CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST env vars must be read alongside the existing ones. After Stack creation on line 69, ContentstackLivePreview.init(Stack) must be called. This is the SETUP site — every downstream fetch depends on this config being present.
  - **Minimal fix:** Add live_preview block to the `options` object (after line 59): `live_preview: { management_token: CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW_TOKEN, enable: CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW === 'true', host: CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST || undefined }`. Add the new env vars to the destructuring block (lines 17-24). After `export const Stack = contentstack.Stack(options);` (line 69), add `ContentstackLivePreview.init(Stack);`. Also add `live_preview` param forwarding in `getEntry`, `getSingleEntry`, `getSingletonEntry` so that when in preview mode the SDK includes draft content. Reuse existing `options` object and `Stack` export pattern.
- **src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx** (`ContentstackProvider`): This is the CARRIER — the React context provider that holds all CMS content and distributes it to every component via `useContentstackContext`/`useContent`. For live preview, this provider must accept an `onEntryChange` callback (from the page's getStaticProps/getServerSideProps) and call `setContent` to trigger re-renders when Contentstack pushes draft updates. Without wiring here, no component will ever see updated draft content.
  - **Minimal fix:** Add `onEntryChange` prop to `IContentStackProviderProps`. Inside ContentstackProvider, register the callback: when called with updated entry data, merge it into `content` state (replace `useMemo` with `useState` + merge logic). The `onEntryChange` callback will be provided by `@contentstack/live-preview-utils`'s `onEntryChange` function, called in each page's getStaticProps/getServerSideProps. Reuse existing `IContentstackContent` interface and `ContentstackContext`.
- **src/services/pageService.ts** (`pageService`): This service orchestrates page-level Contentstack fetches (calling getEntry/getSingleEntry) and is invoked from every page's getStaticProps/getServerSideProps. It must forward the `preview` flag and `live_preview` params to the contentstack service functions, and return the `onEntryChange` callback from `@contentstack/live-preview-utils` so pages can pass it to ContentstackProvider.
  - **Minimal fix:** Add `preview` and `live_preview` parameters to pageService methods. When preview is enabled, pass `live_preview: true` through to `getEntry`/`getSingleEntry`/`getSingletonEntry`. Import `onEntryChange` from `@contentstack/live-preview-utils` and return it alongside the page data so consuming pages can wire it into ContentstackProvider. Reuse existing service method signatures — extend, don't replace.
- **src/hooks/useContent.ts** (`useContent`): This is the primary CONSUMER hook — 60+ components call `useContent().getContentByKey()` to read CMS data from ContentstackContext. Once ContentstackProvider is wired with `onEntryChange` and updates its context state, all components using `useContent` will automatically re-render with draft content. No structural change needed here, but it must be verified that the context update path from ContentstackProvider → ContentstackContext → useContent propagates correctly.
  - **Minimal fix:** No code change required in useContent itself — it already reads from ContentstackContext via `useContentstackContext()`. Verify that when ContentstackProvider updates its `content` state (via onEntryChange), the `getContentByKey` function returns updated values. If ContentstackProvider switches from `useMemo` to `useState`, ensure the `getContentByKey` closure inside useContent still resolves against the latest context value. Reuse existing `useContentstackContext` and `getValue` helper.

## Reviewer Feedback — ADDRESS THESE (a prior code review requested changes)
The team-lead reviewer examined your previous attempt and requested the changes below. This is the highest priority.

A BLOCKER is a required deliverable, not advice. If a blocker says something is MISSING — a test, a file, a case — the only way to resolve it is to CREATE it; leaving it out repeats the rejection. Minimality governs HOW MUCH you write, never WHETHER you write it.

For advisory points: make the smallest edits that resolve each one, and where a point says the change is over-engineered or an existing helper would do, REMOVE the excess rather than adding more.

If you genuinely cannot satisfy a blocker — no seam exists to test against, the behaviour lives entirely in a third-party package — say so explicitly in your final message, naming the blocker and why. An unexplained omission reads as a refusal and will be rejected again.
### BLOCKERS — this attempt is REJECTED until every one is resolved
- [blocker] Both required dependencies @contentstack/live-preview-sdk and @contentstack/live-preview-utils are ABSENT — not declared in package.json and not present in node_modules (verified via dependency_available tool). The implementation calls require('@contentstack/live-preview-sdk') inside a try/catch that silently swallows the ModuleNotFoundError, meaning live preview will silently never initialize in any environment. The prescribed fix explicitly requires these packages. (package.json)
  - Suggested fix: Add @contentstack/live-preview-sdk and @contentstack/live-preview-utils to package.json dependencies and install them. Replace the require() try/catch with a proper ES import so a missing dependency is a build error, not a silent runtime failure.
- [blocker] ContentstackProvider was NOT modified at all (git_state confirms no change to this file). The prescribed minimal fix requires: (1) adding onEntryChange prop to IContentStackProviderProps, (2) switching from useMemo to useState + merge logic so that when Contentstack pushes draft entry updates via the callback, the context state updates and all consuming components re-render. Without this, even if the SDK initializes and pushes draft data, no component will ever display it. This directly fails AC: 'When the page request includes live preview parameters, the rendered page displays the draft content values for the entry being previewed.' (src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx)
  - Suggested fix: Add onEntryChange?: (callback: (entry: IContentstackContent) => void) => void to IContentStackProviderProps. Replace useMemo with useState<IContentstackContent>(defaultContent). In a useEffect, register the onEntryChange callback to merge/replace content state. This is the CARRIER — without it, the entire live preview feature is non-functional.
- [blocker] pageService was NOT modified at all (git_state confirms no change). The prescribed fix requires: (1) adding preview and live_preview parameters to pageService methods, (2) passing live_preview: true through to getEntry/getSingleEntry/findSingletonEntry when preview is enabled, (3) importing onEntryChange from @contentstack/live-preview-utils and returning it alongside page data so consuming pages can wire it into ContentstackProvider. Without this, pages have no way to pass preview params to the contentstack service or receive the onEntryChange callback. This fails AC: 'When the page request includes live preview parameters, the rendered page displays the draft content values.' (src/services/pageService.ts)
  - Suggested fix: Extend pageService method signatures with preview?: boolean and live_preview?: boolean params. When preview is enabled, forward live_preview to the contentstack service calls. Import onEntryChange from @contentstack/live-preview-utils and include it in the return payload so pages can pass it to ContentstackProvider.
- [blocker] The live_preview parameter is destructured in getEntry (line ~150), getSingleEntry (line ~180), and findSingletonEntry (line ~210) but is NEVER actually passed to the Contentstack Query or Entry objects. The ContentstackFactory.createContentTypeQuery and createContentTypeEntryQuery methods do not receive or forward live_preview. This means even with the param in the interface, the SDK will never fetch draft content — the param is dead code. This fails AC: 'When the page request includes live preview parameters, the rendered page displays the draft content values for the entry being previewed.' (src/services/contentstack.ts)
  - Suggested fix: Pass live_preview into the ContentstackFactory methods and call the SDK's query param forwarding (e.g., query.addParam('live_preview', 'true') or the SDK's native .live_preview() chain method — verify the exact API via resolve_package_symbol on the installed package). The param must reach the actual HTTP request to Contentstack.
- [blocker] No logic exists to suppress live preview draft content for unauthenticated visitors on protected pages. AC requires: 'For a page that requires authentication, draft content does not appear on the rendered page when live preview parameters are present and the visitor is unauthenticated.' Since pageService was not modified, there is no guard that checks authentication state before forwarding live_preview params. An unauthenticated visitor on a protected page with live_preview params in the URL would receive draft content if the rest of the pipeline were wired. (src/services/pageService.ts)
  - Suggested fix: In pageService, before forwarding live_preview to contentstack service calls, check whether the page requires authentication and whether the visitor is authenticated. If the page is protected and the visitor is unauthenticated, do NOT forward live_preview (fetch published content only). This may also require coordination with applyMiddlewares or the auth middleware.
- [blocker] No unit tests exist for any of the live preview changes. git_state shows zero test file changes. The prescribed fix touches 3 source files (contentstack.ts, ContentstackContext.tsx, pageService.ts) and none have corresponding vitest tests. All 4 verification criteria lack test coverage: (1) draft content displayed when preview params present, (2) published content displayed when preview not active, (3) unauthenticated visitor cannot view protected page content, (4) draft content does not appear for unauthenticated visitor on protected page. Searched via resolve_test_file conventions and git_state — no test files found or changed. (test/unit/)
  - Suggested fix: Add vitest unit tests mirroring src/ paths: test for contentstack.ts verifying live_preview param forwarding to SDK queries; test for ContentstackContext.tsx verifying onEntryChange callback updates content state and triggers re-render; test for pageService.ts verifying preview param forwarding and auth-gated suppression of live_preview for protected pages. All 4 verification criteria must have explicit it()/test() blocks.
### Advisory — apply where it makes the change smaller or clearer
- [major] Hardcoded string 'api.contentstack.io' used as fallback for CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST. This violates the review criterion: 'No hardcoded strings for model names, endpoint URLs, or file paths — all use named constants from src/config/constants.ts.' (src/services/contentstack.ts)
  - Suggested fix: Add a named constant (e.g., CONTENTSTACK_DEFAULT_PREVIEW_HOST) in src/config/constants.ts and reference it instead of the inline string literal.
