## Root Cause Analysis & Prescribed Fix (AUTHORITATIVE — start here, do not re-trace)
A code investigation already traced this bug to its cause and prescribed the minimal fix below. This is the plan of record. Apply it; do NOT re-read the whole codebase to re-derive it.

The Acceptance Criteria above describe the desired END BEHAVIOR to VERIFY — they are NOT an implementation blueprint. Do not re-architect, split values, or add new fields/abstractions to satisfy an AC literally when the prescribed minimal fix already makes that AC pass. Implement the fix below; the ACs are how you check you got it right.

HARD RULES:
- Make the SMALLEST change that fixes the root cause. Fewer lines of code is always better.
- REUSE existing functions. Before writing any new helper, search the repo for an existing util/parser/formatter that already does what you need (use the CodeGraph tool documented below) and call it. Writing novel code when a helper already exists is a defect to be rejected in review.
- **src/services/contentstack.ts** (`options`): This is the Contentstack Delivery SDK initialization config. The `live_preview` block must be added here (management_token, enable, host) and CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW_TOKEN / CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST env vars must be read alongside the existing ones. After Stack creation on line 69, ContentstackLivePreview.init(Stack) must be called. This is the SETUP site — every downstream fetch depends on this config being present.
  - **Minimal fix:** Add live_preview block to the `options` object (after line 59): `live_preview: { management_token: CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW_TOKEN, enable: CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW === 'true', host: CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST || undefined }`. Add the new env vars to the destructuring block (lines 17-24). After `export const Stack = contentstack.Stack(options);` (line 69), add `ContentstackLivePreview.init(Stack);`. Also add `live_preview` param forwarding in `getEntry`, `getSingleEntry`, `getSingletonEntry` so that when in preview mode the SDK includes draft content. Reuse existing `options` object and `Stack` export pattern.
- **src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx** (`ContentstackProvider`): This is the CARRIER — the React context provider that holds all CMS content and distributes it to every component via `useContentstackContext`/`useContent`. For live preview, this provider must accept an `onEntryChange` callback (from the page's getStaticProps/getServerSideProps) and call `setContent` to trigger re-renders when Contentstack pushes draft updates. Without wiring here, no component will ever see updated draft content.
  - **Minimal fix:** Add `onEntryChange` prop to `IContentStackProviderProps`. Inside ContentstackProvider, register the callback: when called with updated entry data, merge it into `content` state (replace `useMemo` with `useState` + merge logic). The `onEntryChange` callback will be provided by `@contentstack/live-preview-utils`'s `onEntryChange` function, called in each page's getStaticProps/getServerSideProps. Reuse existing `IContentstackContent` interface and `ContentstackContext`.
- **src/services/pageService.ts** (`pageService`): This service orchestrates page-level Contentstack fetches (calling getEntry/getSingleEntry) and is invoked from every page's getStaticProps/getServerSideProps. It must forward the `preview` flag and `live_preview` params to the contentstack service functions, and return the `onEntryChange` callback from `@contentstack/live-preview-utils` so pages can pass it to ContentstackProvider.
  - **Minimal fix:** Add `preview` and `live_preview` parameters to pageService methods. When preview is enabled, pass `live_preview: true` through to `getEntry`/`getSingleEntry`/`getSingletonEntry`. Import `onEntryChange` from `@contentstack/live-preview-utils` and return it alongside the page data so consuming pages can wire it into ContentstackProvider. Reuse existing service method signatures — extend, don't replace.
- **src/hooks/useContent.ts** (`useContent`): This is the primary CONSUMER hook — 60+ components call `useContent().getContentByKey()` to read CMS data from ContentstackContext. Once ContentstackProvider is wired with `onEntryChange` and updates its context state, all components using `useContent` will automatically re-render with draft content. No structural change needed here, but it must be verified that the context update path from ContentstackProvider → ContentstackContext → useContent propagates correctly.
  - **Minimal fix:** No code change required in useContent itself — it already reads from ContentstackContext via `useContentstackContext()`. Verify that when ContentstackProvider updates its `content` state (via onEntryChange), the `getContentByKey` function returns updated values. If ContentstackProvider switches from `useMemo` to `useState`, ensure the `getContentByKey` closure inside useContent still resolves against the latest context value. Reuse existing `useContentstackContext` and `getValue` helper.

