- [major] Uses require() inside a try/catch to load @contentstack/live-preview-sdk, which is an anti-pattern: (1) it bypasses TypeScript type checking, (2) the try/catch silently swallows all errors (not just module-not-found), masking real initialization failures, (3) it prevents tree-shaking. The eslint-disable comment confirms this is intentional but unjustified. (src/services/contentstack.ts)
